## Production feed — what is true today

| Layer | Truth |
|-------|--------|
| **App (baked at pack)** | `OKVEVO_UPDATE_FEED_URL` = `https://releases.okvevo.com/okvevo/stable` from `apps/desktop/scripts/okvevo-feed-urls.mjs` via `ci-map-pack-env.mjs`. Channel `latest` → reads **`latest.yml` / `latest-mac.yml`** under that prefix. |
| **Secret name `PROD_UPDATE_FEED_URL`** | Not used as the baked URL. Mapping **hardcodes** `feedFor('production').url` (`okvevo/stable`). Do not document root as what the app requests. |
| **Publish release** (`okvevo-desktop-publish.yml`) | Points live feed: stable installer names + `releases.json` + root `latest*.yml`, **and** the same live files under `okvevo/stable/` (including Hermes-compat `stable-mac.yml` under the prefix). Smoke checks root **and** `okvevo/stable`. |
| **Website / human downloads** | Stable names: root `OkVevo-mac-arm64.dmg` / `OkVevo-win-x64.exe` after Publish; staging: `okvevo/staging/OkVevo-*`. |
| **Tag pack gap** | `okvevo-desktop-production.yml` archives with `feed_prefix: okvevo/stable` and **`archiveFeed` already writes `okvevo/stable/latest*.yml`**. That can update what production apps read **before** Publish. Tracked in `PRE-LIVE-BACKLOG.md`: “Tag pack writes the live `okvevo/stable/latest*.yml` before Publish release”. Until fixed, treat Publish as the **policy** gate; do not assume tag pack is archive-only for the prefix the app uses. |

**Rule for agents:** one customer updater URL — **`https://releases.okvevo.com/okvevo/stable`**. Only **Publish release** should make a version live; if tag pack still writes that live yml, keep/extend the PRE-LIVE item (do not pretend the gap is closed).

