## Rollback (production)

`allowDowngrade: false` in the app — same-channel numeric downgrade will not auto-install.

| Situation | Action |
|-----------|--------|
| User has **not** updated | Publish release with older archived `version` |
| User **already** updated | Fix-forward: higher patch tag + pack + Publish |
| Manual | Install versioned `OkVevo-{old}-mac-arm64.dmg` / `OkVevo-{old}-win-x64.exe` |

---

## Agent operating rules

1. Ask before commit / push / tag / merge.
2. PRs only into `staging` / `main`; push only `okvevo`.
3. Prefer running `git`, `gh`, curl checks yourself; give Karan numbered console steps only for secrets, Publish release UI, and machine installs.
4. After staging merge → Desktop staging URL + staging download links.
5. After tag push → Desktop production URL; remind Publish is still required for policy / root pointers (and until PRE-LIVE closes, prefix live yml may already have moved).
6. After he publishes → smoke `okvevo/stable` + root stable names.
7. Never invent GitHub Environments for OkVevo-Nia.
8. Never print secrets.
9. Never upload `latest*.yml` before installers pass the HTTPS check.
